---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Disclaimer';
const description = 'World Battery Hub publishes battery information for general reference only — not engineering, purchasing, legal or safety advice.';
const canonical = '/disclaimer/';

const jsonLd = [{
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Disclaimer',
  description,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/disclaimer/',
}];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  dateModified="2026-10-23"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Legal · Last reviewed 2026-10-23</p>
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        World Battery Hub is a battery knowledge and data platform. Everything published here is general
        reference information about battery technology, specifications, testing and markets — it is not
        engineering advice, purchasing advice, legal advice or safety certification for your specific
        application.
      </p>
      <p>
        This disclaimer is issued on behalf of the operator of World Battery Hub — Jinzhou Chengguang Power
        Source Co., Ltd., trading as Chengguang Power Tech — as set out in the
        <a href="/about/#operator-disclosure">operator disclosure</a> on the About page. The disclosure status
        does not change the limits in this disclaimer.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> Use this platform to understand batteries, not to certify a design.
        Verifying a battery for a real installation — sizing, charging, ventilation, protection, transport and
        disposal — is the responsibility of a qualified engineer and of whoever puts the system into service.
        Always follow the battery manufacturer's own documentation, which prevails over anything published here.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Informational purpose only</h2>
      <p>
        Content on this platform — including specifications, equations, calculators, test descriptions,
        manufacturer and market data — is published for general information and education. It is not a
        substitute for professional engineering judgement, a manufacturer's datasheet, a standards document,
        or the advice of a qualified person who has examined your application.
      </p>
      <p>
        No content on this platform should be read as an instruction to install, modify, charge, discharge,
        transport or dispose of a battery in a particular way.
      </p>
      <p>
        "Content" in this disclaimer means everything published on this platform and its sub-sites: editorial
        articles, comparison tables, glossary and reference entries, calculators and tools, compiled datasets,
        manufacturer and market information, and any figure, range or label attached to them. The same limits
        apply to all of it, whatever the format.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No engineering, purchasing or professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        We do not provide engineering, design, installation, maintenance, transport or purchasing advice, and
        nothing on this platform creates a professional relationship of any kind. Calculators and worked
        examples are illustrative models: they use simplified assumptions and are not a substitute for a
        design review, a load study, a protection study or a compliance assessment for your installation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where the platform describes products, manufacturers or market data, that is reference information
        compiled from public sources. It is not a recommendation, endorsement, ranking or suitability
        statement, and it is not a purchasing decision you should make on this platform's word alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        No use of this platform creates a client, advisory, fiduciary or contractual relationship between you
        and the operator of World Battery Hub. Quoting, citing or relying on content here does not make us
        responsible for your project, your product or your decision. You remain responsible for obtaining
        qualified, application-specific advice from a professional who has examined your circumstances.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Safety</h2>
      <p>
        Batteries store energy and can cause injury, fire, chemical burns or property damage if mishandled.
        Lithium batteries can enter thermal runaway; lead-acid batteries contain sulphuric acid and can
        release hydrogen. See our <a href="/safety-notice/">Safety &amp; Liability Notice</a> for the full
        position.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The manufacturer's documentation governs.</strong> Where anything published on this platform
        appears to conflict with the battery manufacturer's instructions, a standards document or your
        jurisdiction's regulations, the manufacturer's instructions and the regulations prevail.
      </p>
      <p>
        Descriptions of hazards, handling and disposal on this platform are general. They do not replace the
        safety data sheet (SDS), the battery's own labelling, the transport documents required for shipping
        hazardous goods (for example UN 3480/3481 for lithium batteries, or UN 2794/2800 for lead-acid), or
        the training required of anyone who handles these products.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Accuracy, completeness and change</h2>
      <p>
        We research content from public sources and cross-check factual claims, as described in our
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>. Even so, battery technology, product lines, standards and
        regulations change continuously, and figures published by third parties can be revised, superseded or
        withdrawn. We give <strong>no warranty</strong> that any content is accurate, complete, current or
        fit for a particular purpose, and we may change, correct or withdraw content at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where figures are uncertain, ranges, approximations or confidence labels are used rather than
        single-value precision. Values presented without a source or a confidence label should be treated as
        indicative only.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party data — manufacturer specifications, market figures, prices, lead times, certifications and
        regulatory requirements — is compiled from the sources stated. We do not warrant that a third party has
        kept a specification current, that a listed certification remains valid, or that a quoted price or
        lead time is still available at the time you read it. A page's review date records our last check, not
        the third party's.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a page is stale or a figure is provisional, we say so on the page rather than presenting it as
        current. If you notice a discrepancy, report it through the
        <a href="/contact/#editorial">editorial correction route</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third-party content, trademarks and links</h2>
      <p>
        Standards, product names, company names and trademarks referenced on this platform belong to their
        respective owners and are used for identification, comparison and explanation only. Their use does not
        imply endorsement, sponsorship, certification or affiliation by either side.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to external websites are provided for reference. We do not control external content and are not
        responsible for its accuracy, availability or practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where we reference a manufacturer, a standard body or a product, the reference is factual, not an
        endorsement. We are not affiliated with any manufacturer, standard body or certification body named on
        this platform unless we say so expressly.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, World Battery Hub and its operators are not liable
        for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential or special loss — including loss of profit,
        business, data or goodwill, damage to equipment or property, personal injury, or costs of
        replacement — arising from the use of, or reliance on, any information published on this platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        This limitation applies however the loss arises, including in contract, tort (including negligence),
        statute or otherwise, and applies whether or not we were advised of the possibility of such loss.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in this disclaimer excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes to this disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this disclaimer as the platform develops. The version published on this page is the
        current version.
      </p>
      <p>
        The review date above records when this disclaimer was last reviewed. Changes take effect when posted,
        and your continued use of the platform after a change means you accept the updated disclaimer.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Governing law and severability</h2>
      <p>
        This disclaimer, and any dispute arising out of or in connection with it or with your use of this
        platform, is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China, without regard to its conflict-of-law
        rules. This is consistent with the <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a>, which contains the full
        governing-law and dispute-resolution position.
      </p>
      <p>
        If any provision of this disclaimer is held to be invalid, illegal or unenforceable by a court or
        competent authority, that provision will be limited or severed to the minimum extent necessary, and the
        remaining provisions will continue in full force and effect. The invalidity of one provision does not
        affect the validity of the others.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in this disclaimer limits or excludes any mandatory right you may have under the law that
        applies to you, including any consumer-protection right that cannot lawfully be waived.
      </p>
      <p>
        This disclaimer is published in English. Where a translation is provided for convenience, the English
        version governs in the event of any difference in meaning.
      </p>
      <p>
        This disclaimer is effective from the review date above and supersedes any earlier version of this
        page. If you have questions about how it applies to you, or believe a specific statement on the
        platform is incorrect, contact us through the <a href="/contact/#editorial">editorial correction
        route</a> before relying on that statement for a safety-critical or commercial decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in this disclaimer is intended to limit any warranty or liability in a way that your applicable
        law prohibits, and each section of this disclaimer is to be read independently so that, if one section
        cannot be enforced, the rest continues to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Related policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> — the terms governing your use of this website.</li>
        <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> — what we collect and why.</li>
        <li><a href="/safety-notice/">Safety &amp; Liability Notice</a> — battery hazards and safety responsibilities.</li>
        <li><a href="/data-use-and-citation/">Data Use &amp; Citation</a> — how our data may be reused and cited.</li>
        <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> — how content is researched, verified and corrected.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="muted">
        Questions about this disclaimer, or a correction to report? Email
        <a href="mailto:editorial@worldbatteryhub.com">editorial@worldbatteryhub.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
